    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW24n2KEq35rjVw9RuL8TYTAi)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on #421 (top of the DEVONthink stack #415 → #418 → #419 → #420 → #421), so it must merge **after #421**.\n  - If merged first, GitHub would target `main` without `sp-devonthink-highlights`, `sp-devonthink-browse` and the #437 crossref resolver: it would not build.\n- Independent of #438 (page labels), #441, #443 and #449: no shared lines except the =sp-devonthink.org= key table (trivial conflict at most).\n- No CHANGELOG edit (the nightly tidy does it).\n\n## What it does\n\n- `C-c k d A` (`sp-devonthink-insert-annotation-link`): asks for a citekey, then inserts a `devonthink:UUID::PAGE` link to one highlight of the record's PDF.\n  - Two modes: `latest` (most recently created highlight) or `choose` (completing-read: page, creation date, text, comment).\n  - `sp-devonthink-annotation-default` (`choose`) sets the mode; a prefix argument takes the other.\n- `C-c k d L` (`sp-devonthink-insert-latest-annotation-link`): the thin command for `latest`.\n- Uses `sp-devonthink-record` (#437), so a chapter without its own record lists the parent book's highlights (a message says so).\n- `tools/devonthink-highlights.py --annotations` prints every highlight with page, text, comment, creation and modification date (PyMuPDF).\n- Link format is unchanged, so `org-open` and export work as before.\n\n## Assumed, not verified (not run on the Mac)\n\n- DEVONthink's AppleScript only gives an annotation *count* per record, not the annotations; so highlights are read from the PDF file, as in #420.\n- The link opens the **page** of the highlight, not the highlight itself: I know no DEVONthink URL parameter that selects an annotation.\n- Assumes DEVONthink writes its highlights into the file as standard highlight annotations with a `/CreationDate`.\n  - Without a creation date the modification date is used; without either, the last one in the file counts as \"latest\".\n- Assumes a highlight made in DEVONthink is saved to the file straight away (it may only appear after the PDF is closed).\n- Page labels (#438) do not apply on this base: pages are physical PDF pages, which is what `?page=` uses. Showing printed pages in the list is a follow-up once #438 is merged.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/sp-devonthink-highlights-test.el`: 19 pass (10 new; AppleScript and `call-process` stubbed).\n- `tests/sp-devonthink-test.el`: 31 pass.\n- `tests/test_devonthink_highlights.py`: 8 pass (incl. a real PDF with a dated, commented highlight).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `M-x sp-devonthink-insert-annotation-link` in an Org buffer, pick a citekey whose PDF has highlights: the list shows page, date and text in file order.\n- [ ] Choose one: a `[[devonthink:…::N][key p. N]]` link is inserted and opens DEVONthink on page N.\n- [ ] `C-u C-c k d A` (or `C-c k d L`): the most recently made highlight is linked, without a question.\n- [ ] Make a new highlight in DEVONthink, then run `C-c k d L` again: is it picked (check whether it needs the PDF closed first)?\n- [ ] A chapter citekey with no record of its own: the parent's record is used and the message appears.\n- [ ] A citekey with no highlights, and one with no record: a clear `user-error`.\n- [ ] Highlights with a comment show it in brackets; one without a date shows `----------`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCS4JXTFeKTVZdyCgR)_",
